                        <p> See: The trial of James Gillham, an attorney, for demanding and
                                receiving of Lord Falkland, Henry Speed, Esq. and D. Broughton, Esq. the
                                sum of three hundred twenty-two pounds, … Tried in the Court of King's
                                Bench, Westminster, on the 20<sup>th</sup> of February, 1795 … taken in short hand, by
                                Manoah Sibley.</p>
                            <p>Reported in the Whitehall Eevening Post Feb 24, 1795 - an indictment,
                                preferred by Lord Falkland, for taking, in the character of a money
                                broker, more than 10s for every 100l. contrary to the statute. </p>
